A||||9||btoth||Messed up GT accelleration||||9||
Z||000000||btoth||06-14-2000||05:35 PM||||I have an 86 GT (automatic).  it lacks all power when accelerating - even when flooring the gas pedal.  at first i thought that it was a timming issue because when i would speed up the timming (turning the distributor counter clockwise) it would accellerate much faster but the shift points were still screwed up.  i thought that maybe the timming chain could be worn out and maybe that was messing with the timming so i asked my mechanic and he said that the timming chain should be fine seeing as how it only has 87000 miles on it.  the engine was rebuilt a few months ago because of leaking head gaskets (this was done professionally) and just about all sensors have been replaced recently (thottle pos., temp, oxygen sensor....).  so now i have the timming set to the 10 degree mark like it says on the underside of the deck lid.  could this be a computer problem?  (i've tried reseting the computer many times)  or is it probably just something stupid like a bad sensor (tach filter sensor?  bad t.p sensor?)   sorry this is so long.  thanks in advance for any ideas.  :O)||||reg||9
Z||000001||Jim's87GT||06-14-2000||06:00 PM||||The problems with acceleration on my 87GT were related to a clogged catalytic converter.  I had replaced the plugs, wires, rotor, dist. cap and got no change.  I replaced the air filter and that was no help.  I thought it might be the cat but couldn't loosen the clamps to it, so I took off the EGR to check.  (I should note that the engine wouldn't rev over 2,800 RPM) when I tried it with the EGR off it idled at 4,500 RPM (BIG vacuum leak!!).  I replaced the cat and it runs fine.  Try loosening the EGR and see what happens.||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||06-14-2000||07:29 PM||||thanks.   i had considered a clogged catalytic converter.  it had been leaking oil and coolent very bad and after the rebuild it cleared out even more coolent through the pipes.  and it is the original so there's probably a good chance that it needs to be replaced...||||reg||7
Z||000003||Ed||06-14-2000||08:23 PM||||My experience is that a general lack of power is usually related to induction or fuel (air filter, fuel filter, injectors) and misfire is electrical (all generalizations, of course).  <P>So I'd agree to look at "cat" function, air filter, fuel filter first.  A clogged "cat" may also result in the recently much discussed red exhaust manifolds.    ||||reg||1
Z||000004||LarryB||06-14-2000||11:57 PM||||Could be your transmission is slipping? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||06-15-2000||06:17 AM||||The bad shifting is what would make me lean towards a timing or tranny issue.  I assume you know how to properly time a Fiero(you ARE jumpering the connectors right?)  I know from experience that a 'retarded' motor WILL cause your shifts to feel very akward.  The clogged cat sounds very possible, but how bout checking the tranny fluid?  Is it at the proper level, and does it look and smell good?  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||btoth||06-15-2000||10:29 AM||||yeah, i checked the trans. fluid - looks fine, doesn't really smell (at least not like it's bad.)  yeah, i jumpered the connectors.  my timming light said that it was at the 10 degree mark... (maybe the timming light is messed up?  is this possible?)  i know that when i speed up the timming it does run a lot  better.  but i still think that something else is wrong (cat. converter, sensor, comp.) - but i'm going to try the catalytic converter before more sensors and before i mess with the timming again since it's probably about time for a new one anyway - it couldn't hurt.||||reg||1
Z||000007||btoth||06-15-2000||05:26 PM||||YAY!!!  i just picked my car up from midas... new catalytic converter fixed all my problems.  it's so freakin' fast now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">)   thanks for the help!||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT Bastard||06-15-2000||09:27 PM||||Hell yeah, man!  That's what the forum is all about.||||reg||12
Z||000009||contra||06-16-2000||09:26 PM||||check your ignition module too<BR>when mine started to go on my '85 i almost thought i blew my transmission racing the darn thing, it scared me for a bit until my mechanic told me what really was wrong.<BR>I makes it feel like when you step on the gas, that the power just drops and the car doesn't go anywhere <BR>just a thought<BR>||||reg||3
